      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14264509/assets/0e2f2a41a551f21727825514a83dd8a0df4b45d8ea790f05e1e63d6a6e784526.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following is the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{2}f(x)?$\n\n(*Note: Figures not drawn to scale*)",
      "worked_solution": "To graph the function $y=\\frac{1}{2}f(x),$ we take the graph of $y=f(x)$ and compress it by factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis. This has the effect of dividing the $y$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(x)$ by $2.$\n\nThe resulting graph is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14264509/assets/dc03088ce43bd35e758a49278288c0c22e31d0d48682dd7280c9b21b3353cece.png)",
